# The ARM3 release line through its pulse limiter (dfb89499, F; G1 05:05 (1)(b); F′ 12 gt, ironfarm
# 07:25): L1 (ARM3) fires A, the stone moves into B (t 4), the latch's comparator Q reads B: strength
# 1 (one stone in a 9-slot dropper) at R1's input (t 6); C pulses once, 12 gt (t 10..21); L1 again (a
# rolled-back re-press) fires A empty: nothing; L2 (the REL SET stand-in) fires B, the stone returns
# (t 54 after its flip), the level falls: nothing on C. Then the SECOND rise (G1 on F, non-blocking):
# L1 off and on again fires A, the stone back in B, and the limiter, re-armed, pulses again: 12 gt on
# the release line's end o (the output dust), q high again.
# THE RELEASE PULSE WIDTH: 12 gt, an INTERFACE value (G1 07:27 (1)(b) / 07:37 (3): stated once in
# day-1's controller interface, designs/farms/iron/carousel-assembly/wip/controller/
# f1q2-day1-controller-interface.md at d44c9f19d64817ab5bdc43a2158323d3fb5f9cd9 (explore/day1-tools),
# "## Interface values": "release pulse = 12 gt", the one state source this limiter's side branch
# (the delay-2 + delay-4 repeaters) and day-1's napper trim both read); C's and o's traces below check
# it (12 characters on).
design designs/gadgets/arm3-release-limiter.txt
probe_items b 2 1 0
probe_items a 3 1 0
probe q 2 1 1
probe_signal qin 2 1 2
probe c 2 1 4
probe out 2 1 5
use 4 1 0
trace 6
expect b 1
expect qin 1
expect_trace c 0001111111111110000
expect q 1
use 4 1 0
use 4 1 0
expect_trace c 0000000000000000000000000
expect b 1
use 1 1 0
expect_trace c 0000000000000000000000000
expect a 1
expect qin 0
expect q 0
use 4 1 0
use 4 1 0
expect_trace out 000000000++++++++++++0000
expect b 1
expect q 1
